WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:02.710
- [Narrator] Okay, so here
are three rules to live by

00:00:02.710 --> 00:00:04.640
that will quickly improve your life.

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:08.170
Rule number one, follow the
path of most resistance.

00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:11.130
Now, this obviously
isn't an absolute rule,

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:13.400
like you probably have a lot of resistance

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:15.900
towards driving into oncoming traffic

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:18.270
or throwing your laptop into a lake,

00:00:18.270 --> 00:00:19.710
and that's probably a good thing.

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:22.470
But if you have two brain
cells to rub together,

00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:23.500
then you probably know

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:25.170
that's not what I'm talking about here.

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:28.110
I'm talking about the
internal resistance you feel

00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:30.880
when you think about doing
something constructive,

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:32.930
something that would
move your life forward

00:00:32.930 --> 00:00:34.320
in some way or another,

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:35.630
like writing a cover letter

00:00:35.630 --> 00:00:38.220
for a job posting you've
been keeping an eye on,

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:40.740
or finally cleaning your
hell hole of a garage

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:43.240
where you've been stashing
eight months of cardboard.

00:00:43.240 --> 00:00:45.970
This type of internal
resistance that you feel

00:00:45.970 --> 00:00:48.240
when you think about
taking care of these things

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:50.200
is also the same type of resistance

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:52.830
that feels empowering to overcome,

00:00:52.830 --> 00:00:55.270
but paralyzing if we stay under its thumb.

00:00:55.270 --> 00:00:58.160
But if we can learn to not
shy away from this feeling,

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:00.200
but instead lean into it,

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:02.720
we will find that our
life will rapidly improve

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:05.120
because the most rewarding things in life

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:08.740
are hidden behind discomfort
or resistance paywalls.

00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:12.500
We purchase long-lasting
order and success in our lives

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:14.270
through temporary discomfort,

00:01:14.270 --> 00:01:17.690
and if we become aware of
this weird little transaction

00:01:17.690 --> 00:01:20.900
that seems to be deeply woven
into the fabric of reality,

00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:22.950
we can use it to our advantage.

00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:25.310
We can be comfortable
with making this trade

00:01:25.310 --> 00:01:26.800
as often as possible.

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:29.670
And one thing that I've noticed
is that as we get better

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:33.180
at willingly leaning into
this discomfort of action,

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:34.013
after a while,

00:01:34.013 --> 00:01:37.120
we'll actually start to enjoy
the feeling of resistance.

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:38.370
It's kind of a weird thing.

00:01:38.370 --> 00:01:41.860
The discomfort itself becomes
exciting and empowering.

00:01:41.860 --> 00:01:45.140
I think this is because
since resistance is a source

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:47.510
of power after we transcend it,

00:01:47.510 --> 00:01:49.330
then once we go through this process

00:01:49.330 --> 00:01:51.490
of transcending it frequently enough,

00:01:51.490 --> 00:01:53.570
our brain eventually starts to clue in.

00:01:53.570 --> 00:01:56.690
We'll just link this feeling
of discomfort with empowerment,

00:01:56.690 --> 00:02:00.140
and we'll get excited to overcome
obstacles and challenges.

00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:01.470
Remember this rule.

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:04.670
When we overcome resistance,
we absorb its power.

00:02:04.670 --> 00:02:07.300
The greater the resistance,
the greater the power.

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:10.130
Rule number two, don't
stop doing the things

00:02:10.130 --> 00:02:12.430
that got you out of a bad situation.

00:02:12.430 --> 00:02:13.330
Kind of a mouthful.

00:02:13.330 --> 00:02:15.130
But what I mean is that human beings

00:02:15.130 --> 00:02:16.680
are pretty hilarious sometimes.

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:18.710
It's because most of
the time we know exactly

00:02:18.710 --> 00:02:21.390
what we need to do to
stop feeling like crap,

00:02:21.390 --> 00:02:23.680
like if we've worked
ourselves into a hole,

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:26.100
we're playing more video
games, we're eating junk food,

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:27.150
blabbity blabbity blah,

00:02:27.150 --> 00:02:29.150
and we're just not
taking care of ourselves,

00:02:29.150 --> 00:02:31.010
we're in this negative mindset,

00:02:31.010 --> 00:02:32.690
this self-loathing spiral.

00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:35.640
Eventually this goes on for
a long enough period of time

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:37.360
that we eventually snap.

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:38.300
We say, "You know what?

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:40.860
I'm tired of living my
life like a piece of crap.

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:42.380
I'm gonna change things up."

00:02:42.380 --> 00:02:43.650
So we bounce back.

00:02:43.650 --> 00:02:46.210
We start eating better,
we start going to the gym,

00:02:46.210 --> 00:02:47.987
we start getting our work done on time,

00:02:47.987 --> 00:02:49.800
and we start showering in the morning

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:51.840
and dressing into something half decent.

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:54.510
And as we do this, we start
to feel better and better.

00:02:54.510 --> 00:02:56.090
We start to feel more confident,

00:02:56.090 --> 00:02:58.980
we start to feel more energized
and better about ourselves.

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:01.670
But the weird thing is
something usually happens.

00:03:01.670 --> 00:03:04.450
Since we no longer have
that negative incentive

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:06.490
to work ourselves out of the hole,

00:03:06.490 --> 00:03:09.270
we kind of forget why we
were taking care of ourselves

00:03:09.270 --> 00:03:10.103
to begin with.

00:03:10.103 --> 00:03:11.260
So we start to slip.

00:03:11.260 --> 00:03:12.400
We cut corners.

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:14.060
We skip the gym one day.

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:16.360
That turns into two days,
which turns into a week,

00:03:16.360 --> 00:03:17.193
into a month,

00:03:17.193 --> 00:03:19.800
and we eventually slip and
slide down the slippery

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:22.000
and slidey slope back into the hole

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:23.120
from whence we came.

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:25.980
But have you ever considered
what your life might look like

00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:28.040
if you didn't stop doing the things

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:29.830
that got you out of a bad situation?

00:03:29.830 --> 00:03:32.710
Because in reality, there's
no secret to success.

00:03:32.710 --> 00:03:36.780
Success isn't built by doing
lavish, extraordinary things

00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:39.420
like banging out an entire book overnight,

00:03:39.420 --> 00:03:41.960
200 brilliant pages of literature,

00:03:41.960 --> 00:03:44.680
and it's not by going to the
gym harder than everyone else

00:03:44.680 --> 00:03:47.320
that one time you're
motivated to go to the gym.

00:03:47.320 --> 00:03:50.300
You work out so hard that
one day you just explode

00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:51.670
into this meat mountain.

00:03:51.670 --> 00:03:52.900
No, it's ridiculous.

00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:55.810
Success is built by doing the same things

00:03:55.810 --> 00:03:57.850
that got us out of our rut,

00:03:57.850 --> 00:04:00.460
but just continuing to
do those same things

00:04:00.460 --> 00:04:03.080
every single day, over
a long period of time.

00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:06.010
The key is to just do
these things long enough

00:04:06.010 --> 00:04:08.130
that they get locked in as habits.

00:04:08.130 --> 00:04:11.420
Habits, meaning that they're
easier to do than not to do,

00:04:11.420 --> 00:04:13.280
because that's what
happens when you engage

00:04:13.280 --> 00:04:15.230
with these things for long enough.

00:04:15.230 --> 00:04:18.000
They'll eventually just
become a part of who you are

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:20.470
and they'll be easier
to do than not to do.

00:04:20.470 --> 00:04:22.670
And if this sounds kind
of miserable to you,

00:04:22.670 --> 00:04:25.340
just know that it doesn't
have to be such a grind

00:04:25.340 --> 00:04:27.370
because as I've mentioned previously,

00:04:27.370 --> 00:04:29.960
eventually doing these constructive things

00:04:29.960 --> 00:04:31.230
feels really good.

00:04:31.230 --> 00:04:32.520
On a long enough timeline,

00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:34.560
you'll begin to look
forward to these things,

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:36.070
not as a means to an end,

00:04:36.070 --> 00:04:38.200
but because of the way they make you feel.

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:39.380
So start small,

00:04:39.380 --> 00:04:41.480
try to implement one simple habit

00:04:41.480 --> 00:04:43.510
that you actually think
you're gonna stick to,

00:04:43.510 --> 00:04:46.420
lock it in for 30 days
or however long it takes

00:04:46.420 --> 00:04:48.400
until you feel like it's really sticking,

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:49.970
and then add a new habit.

00:04:49.970 --> 00:04:51.960
And keep on doing that
until you're in a place

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:54.870
where you feel satisfied
with your daily life

00:04:54.870 --> 00:04:57.470
and the activities that
you do on a daily basis.

00:04:57.470 --> 00:04:59.930
That's different for everybody,
but use your judgment.

00:04:59.930 --> 00:05:02.900
Okay, rule number three,
record everything.

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:04.820
So life can be pretty turbulent.

00:05:04.820 --> 00:05:08.340
Some days, life really
just deals you a shit hand

00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:11.170
and maybe something truly
devastating happens to you

00:05:11.170 --> 00:05:12.640
and it rocks your world

00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:14.180
and you have no idea what to do.

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:16.690
And other times you have an amazing day.

00:05:16.690 --> 00:05:19.130
You feel euphoric, on top of the world.

00:05:19.130 --> 00:05:20.870
You think to yourself, "Holy smokes.

00:05:20.870 --> 00:05:22.700
Why don't I feel like this more often?"

00:05:22.700 --> 00:05:24.960
Instead of remaining completely oblivious

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:26.720
as to why you feel good or bad,

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:28.860
why not start writing stuff down

00:05:28.860 --> 00:05:30.710
and recording your thoughts and feelings

00:05:30.710 --> 00:05:32.060
on a day-to-day basis?

00:05:32.060 --> 00:05:35.170
Because when you do this,
patterns start to emerge.

00:05:35.170 --> 00:05:38.050
You start to realize that
there's an intimate relationship

00:05:38.050 --> 00:05:39.920
between your repeated behaviors

00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:41.650
and the way that they make you feel.

00:05:41.650 --> 00:05:45.140
So I truly believe one of
the best bang-for-buck habits

00:05:45.140 --> 00:05:48.760
you can start implementing is
just recording your thoughts,

00:05:48.760 --> 00:05:51.790
either as a voice memo
or as a written document

00:05:51.790 --> 00:05:53.630
on a piece of paper or a notebook.

00:05:53.630 --> 00:05:56.910
Because once we start verbalizing
or writing things down,

00:05:56.910 --> 00:05:57.900
taking our thoughts

00:05:57.900 --> 00:06:01.030
out of the weird
cobweb-ridden nest in our head

00:06:01.030 --> 00:06:03.430
and manifesting them into the real world,

00:06:03.430 --> 00:06:05.210
as woo-woo as that sounds,

00:06:05.210 --> 00:06:07.730
it's easier to see our
thoughts for what they are.

00:06:07.730 --> 00:06:11.510
And once our thoughts and
behaviors are actually recorded

00:06:11.510 --> 00:06:12.820
in an objective way,

00:06:12.820 --> 00:06:14.240
then it becomes really difficult

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:16.400
to keep making the same mistakes.

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:18.447
You'll start to eventually clue in that,

00:06:18.447 --> 00:06:21.150
"Oh, when I do this, I feel like that.

00:06:21.150 --> 00:06:23.100
When I think these types of thoughts,

00:06:23.100 --> 00:06:24.570
it makes me feel like this."

00:06:24.570 --> 00:06:27.100
And hypothetically, yeah,
I think you can come

00:06:27.100 --> 00:06:29.770
to these conclusions without
writing these things down,

00:06:29.770 --> 00:06:31.990
but why make this process of growing

00:06:31.990 --> 00:06:34.800
as a person any slower
than it needs to be?

00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:36.920
And no matter whether you're
recording your thoughts

00:06:36.920 --> 00:06:39.650
and feelings from a good day or a bad day,

00:06:39.650 --> 00:06:42.200
all information is good information.

00:06:42.200 --> 00:06:44.560
Use this information to your benefit

00:06:44.560 --> 00:06:46.730
and your life will dramatically improve.

00:06:46.730 --> 00:06:47.970
So that's pretty much it.

00:06:47.970 --> 00:06:51.030
These three rules have
really helped me in my life

00:06:51.030 --> 00:06:52.890
and I really hope they help you as well.

